{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Take all the chiefs of the people and impale them.</b> This command is not to put to death the chiefs of the people, but those who clung to the assembly of the chiefs — and this is what Onkelos translated: 'and judge and kill those liable to execution,' and he did not translate 'and kill them.' So too it mentions in the matter of the calf: 'And Moses said to the judges of Israel: each man slay his men' — and the judges of Israel are the chiefs of the people. And even though Scripture did not explicitly state that the judges did so, since the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded Moses and Moses commanded the judges, it is implied that they did so. Or one may say that they did not have time to do so before Pinchas arose and performed this deed suddenly, with great zeal and dispatch — and immediately the plague was stayed." "<b>To YHWH.</b> To sanctify the Name of Heaven. <b>Before the sun.</b> That the Name be sanctified in public, just as they profaned it in public. Or one may say 'before the sun' because they sinned at Peor, against the attribute of Jacob, who is called 'sun' — as they said in the Midrash: 'Said Jacob: Who told this one that my name is Sun?' Therefore it was necessary to say 'before the sun,' so that their punishment would be from the same source as their sin. Or one may say 'before the sun' — as long as the sun is in the world; once it sets, they are to be buried, from what is written (Deuteronomy 21:23): 'his body shall not remain all night upon the tree.'" "<b>And in the Midrash,</b> 'before the sun' — Moses said before the Holy One, blessed be He: Master of the universe, who informs me of those who clung? He said to him: I will make them known. The cloud would fold back and the sun would shine upon every person who had sinned, and they would hang him immediately."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:01.443148512Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}